  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If Rest in Peace is destroyed by a spell, Rest in Peace will be exiled and then the spell will be put into its owner's graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card is discarded while Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that function when a card is discarded (such as madness) still work, even though that card never reaches a graveyard. In addition, spells or abilities that check the characteristics of a discarded card (such as Chandra Ablaze's first ability) can find that card in exile.",
      "oracle_id": "087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that trigger whenever a creature dies won't trigger because cards and tokens are never put into a player's graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It counts how many cards you discard. Since this card will not be in your hand at that time, this card is not counted.",
      "oracle_id": "686cce6e-18ec-45b0-8d2e-74fa353a905e",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If more than one card is discarded due to a single effect, the Library allows you to decide whether or not to use it on each of the cards. You get to decide the order the cards are placed on the library if more than one goes there.",
      "oracle_id": "867def48-4be8-4056-bcf1-d6b00450b9a3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Since the card goes directly to the library, the card is not revealed unless the spell or ability requiring the discard specifically says it is.",
      "oracle_id": "867def48-4be8-4056-bcf1-d6b00450b9a3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The ability applies any time a spell or ability has you discard as part of its effect. It does not matter if you or your opponent control the spell or ability. The discard is forced because it is an effect.",
      "oracle_id": "867def48-4be8-4056-bcf1-d6b00450b9a3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The ability replaces the normal discard action with a discard action that puts the card on the library instead of the graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "867def48-4be8-4056-bcf1-d6b00450b9a3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The discard triggers anything else that triggers on discards.",
      "oracle_id": "867def48-4be8-4056-bcf1-d6b00450b9a3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This effect has no effect on the cards being put into the graveyard from a library, because they are not \"discarded\".",
      "oracle_id": "867def48-4be8-4056-bcf1-d6b00450b9a3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can look at a randomly discarded card before deciding where it goes.",
      "oracle_id": "867def48-4be8-4056-bcf1-d6b00450b9a3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't use the Library of Leng ability to place a discarded card on top of your library when you discard a card as a cost, because costs aren't effects.",
      "oracle_id": "867def48-4be8-4056-bcf1-d6b00450b9a3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If multiple effects modify your hand size, apply them in timestamp order. For example, if you put Null Profusion (an enchantment that says your maximum hand size is two) onto the battlefield and then put Library of Leng onto the battlefield, you'll have no maximum hand size. However, if those permanents entered in the opposite order, your maximum hand size would be two.",
      "oracle_id": "867def48-4be8-4056-bcf1-d6b00450b9a3",
      "published_at": "2009-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an opponent hasn't drawn any cards in a turn and a spell or ability instructs that player to draw multiple cards, that player will just draw one card. However, if the draws are optional, the player can't choose to draw, even if they could draw one card this way.",
      "oracle_id": "ab26fbe2-e808-48b9-8d0d-3fbb6c3d554f",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Narset will \"see\" cards drawn by opponents earlier in the turn she entered the battlefield, although Narset can't affect cards drawn before she entered the battlefield. For example, if an opponent draws two cards, then Narset enters the battlefield, that opponent can't draw more cards that turn, but the two drawn cards are unaffected.",
      "oracle_id": "ab26fbe2-e808-48b9-8d0d-3fbb6c3d554f",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Replacement effects (such as that of Underrealm Lich or the first ability of Jace, Wielder of Mysteries) can't be used to replace draws that Narset disallows. However, if an opponent's first draw is replaced (by Underrealm Lich's ability, for example), that draw didn't happen and Narset won't stop the next draw (which may also be replaced by Underrealm Lich's ability).",
      "oracle_id": "ab26fbe2-e808-48b9-8d0d-3fbb6c3d554f",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Your opponents can each draw a maximum of one card each on each player's turn. Subsequent card draws during that turn are ignored.",
      "oracle_id": "ab26fbe2-e808-48b9-8d0d-3fbb6c3d554f",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a player had one card or no cards in their hand, that player won't draw any cards.",
      "oracle_id": "c527eb80-ccac-40b8-8377-c31121613128",
      "published_at": "2014-11-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Dredge can replace any card draw, not only the one during your draw step.",
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect puts a card into your hand without specifically using the word \"draw,\" you're not drawing a card. Dredge can't replace this event.",
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you're drawing multiple cards, each draw is performed one at a time. For example, if you're instructed to draw two cards and you replace the first draw with a dredge ability, another card with a dredge ability (including one that was milled by the first dredge ability) may be used to replace the second draw.",
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once you've announced that you're applying a card's dredge ability to replace a draw, players can't take any actions until you've put that card into your hand and milled cards.",
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "One card draw can't be replaced by multiple dredge abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't attempt to use a dredge ability if you don't have enough cards in your library.",
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Notably, Stinkweed Imp's ability isn't deathtouch. It's a triggered ability that triggers only on combat damage.",
      "oracle_id": "e005bc76-4985-4ec6-b9f6-cf6d0d9f5df4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Dredge can replace any card draw, not only the one during your draw step.",
      "oracle_id": "e005bc76-4985-4ec6-b9f6-cf6d0d9f5df4",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect puts a card into your hand without specifically using the word \"draw,\" you're not drawing a card. Dredge can't replace this event.",
      "oracle_id": "e005bc76-4985-4ec6-b9f6-cf6d0d9f5df4",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you're drawing multiple cards, each draw is performed one at a time. For example, if you're instructed to draw two cards and you replace the first draw with a dredge ability, another card with a dredge ability (including one that was milled by the first dredge ability) may be used to replace the second draw.",
      "oracle_id": "e005bc76-4985-4ec6-b9f6-cf6d0d9f5df4",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once you've announced that you're applying a card's dredge ability to replace a draw, players can't take any actions until you've put that card into your hand and milled cards.",
      "oracle_id": "e005bc76-4985-4ec6-b9f6-cf6d0d9f5df4",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "One card draw can't be replaced by multiple dredge abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "e005bc76-4985-4ec6-b9f6-cf6d0d9f5df4",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't attempt to use a dredge ability if you don't have enough cards in your library.",
      "oracle_id": "e005bc76-4985-4ec6-b9f6-cf6d0d9f5df4",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn’t provide any additional benefit.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it’s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don’t grant bonuses to your opponents’ Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card has {X} in its mana cost, you must choose 0 as the value of X when casting it without paying its mana cost.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an attacking creature has multiple evasion abilities, such as shadow and flying, a creature can block it only if that creature satisfies all of the appropriate evasion abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you cast a card this way, you may not cast it for any other alternative costs it has, but you may pay for additional costs, such as kicker costs. If the spell requires an additional cost, you must pay that cost.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If your opponent discards a card while you control Dauthi Voidwalker, abilities that function when that card is discarded still work, even though that card never reaches that player's graveyard. In addition, spells or abilities that check the characteristics of the discarded card can find that card in exile.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Playing a card with Dauthi Voidwalker's last ability is still subject to normal timing restrictions.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tokens still die while Dauthi Voidwalker is on the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While Dauthi Voidwalker is on the battlefield, nontoken creatures your opponents control won't die. They'll be exiled instead. Abilities that would trigger when those creatures die won't trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an opponent is instructed to draw a card then discard a card, and Notion Thief causes you to draw a card instead, that opponent still discards a card. The same is true of any other actions that opponent is instructed to do.",
      "oracle_id": "f8dab16e-1d50-443e-9431-8b6f1cf61c9c",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If two or more players each control a Notion Thief and a player would draw a card other than the first one in their draw step, that player chooses one of the applicable Notion Thief effects to apply. Then the player whose Notion Thief's effect was chosen repeats this process among the remaining Notion Thief effects, and so on, until there are no more possible such effects to apply. Each effect can be applied to the card draw only once this way.",
      "oracle_id": "f8dab16e-1d50-443e-9431-8b6f1cf61c9c",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The above procedure means that if each player in a two-player game controls a Notion Thief and one would draw a card, it really will be that player who draws a card.",
      "oracle_id": "f8dab16e-1d50-443e-9431-8b6f1cf61c9c",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
